# Substance 3D Designer nodes reference for Houdini 22 Copernicus height ports (11 October 2026)

Contract: this file is part 05 of the HEIGHT map porting dataset. It documents the Adobe Substance 3D Designer compositing graph nodes (atomic nodes and the node library) so that a procedural height map built in Designer can be rebuilt with real Copernicus (COP) nodes of Houdini 22.0.368. (11 October 2026)

Sources: the official Adobe documentation on Experience League (the successor of the helpx.adobe.com pages), read from the English documentation repository published by Adobe (default branch dated 8 October 2026, which includes Designer 16.0 from 14 April 2026), plus the local Houdini 22.0.368 COP node help and the SideFX page "Copernicus for Substance 3D Designer users". (11 October 2026)

Method: every purpose, usage note and parameter explanation below is written in my own words; node names and parameter names are exact facts copied from the documentation. Ranges are shown as documented (a hyphen range such as 0 - 32 is rewritten as 0 to 32). (11 October 2026)

Evidence levels: an equivalence marked SideFX-confirmed is a node-level correspondence stated by SideFX. Everything else about Copernicus is my inference and is marked UNVERIFIED. COP node names were checked automatically against the authoritative Houdini 22.0.368 COP node list, and COP parameter labels (shown in bold) were checked against the local node help. (11 October 2026)

Notation: SD parameters and COP node internal names are in backticks, COP parameter labels are in bold, COP input and output ports are written as "name input" or "name output". (11 October 2026)


