### Cells 1 (11 October 2026)
- Category: Texture generators > Noises (11 October 2026)
- Height relevance: high (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/node-library/texture-generators/noises/cells-1 (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: Scatters a selectable shape in every grid cell and overlays the shapes with a Max blend, producing varied cell-like blobs. (11 October 2026)
- Key parameters: (11 October 2026)
  - `Scale` (Integer): Grid subdivision; more cells and smaller shapes at higher values. (11 October 2026)
  - `Pattern` (Integer): The base shape scattered in each cell. (11 October 2026)
  - `Pattern size` (Float2): Size multiplier per axis relative to the cell (1.0 spans the whole cell). (11 October 2026)
  - `Pattern scale` (Float): Uniform multiplier on top of Pattern size. (11 October 2026)
  - `Luminance random` (Float): Range of random darkening per cell, 1 being the full range. (11 October 2026)
  - `Angle` (Float): Direction of the shapes in turns, starting from horizontal right. (11 October 2026)
  - `Angle random` (Float): Maximum random variation of the angle, in turns. (11 October 2026)
- Other parameters (names only): `Disorder`, `Disorder speed`, `Disorder anisotropy`, `Disorder anisotropy angle`, `Tile offset`, `Non-square expansion` (11 October 2026)
- Typical use in a height graph: Pebbles, cobblestones, scales, bumps and cell-like relief; the per-cell luminance random gives height variation between stones. (11 October 2026)
- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `cellularnoise` (use the `noise` output output, **Jitter**, **Bevel**, **Smooth Edge**, **Mode**=Relative) or `cellpattern` which adds per-cell **Random Height**, **Rotate** and **Distort**; for arbitrary stamp shapes use `shapescatter`. (11 October 2026)
- Equivalence status: UNVERIFIED (mapping and parameter values inferred by me; COP node names checked against the Houdini 22.0.368 node list, parameter labels read in the local node help) (11 October 2026)

